## carts-mass

carts-mass-ask = How can two carts’ masses be compared without weighing them?
carts-mass-title = Mass as the measure of inertia and gravity: carts
carts-mass-question = Two light 100 g carts stand on the table with a squeezed spring between them, tied by a thread. We burn the thread — the spring pushes the carts apart, and by the video’s frames we measure how far each went in 0.5 s. First the carts are alike, then one and then two 100 g weights go on the second. At last both carts hang on a dynamometer. How can two carts’ masses be compared without weighing them?
carts-mass-choices = By the speeds after the push: as many times slower a cart is, so many times greater its mass
carts-mass-choices-2 = No way: one spring pushes both carts alike, so they go alike
carts-mass-choices-3 = The heavier cart goes faster — it gathers more speed
carts-mass-setup = Two light 100 g carts, a spring between them, a thread and matches, 100 g weights, a ruler, a phone camera, a dynamometer (up to 5 N)
